    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and routed all household-keyed logic through it, keeping each edit inside a small, low-complexity class.\n\n**Core change**\n- `HouseholdId.of(lastName, postcode)` now returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (was a `hashCode` over lastName+address).\n\n**Callers updated to feed postcode / stay consistent**\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 `householdId` and `identityKey` expressions now pass `owner.getPostcode()`.\n- `IdentityKey.of` \u2014 4th param renamed `address \u2192 postcode`, forwarded to `HouseholdId`.\n\n**Behavioural changes for the spec**\n- `RequireUniqueHousehold` \u2014 rewritten to reject a create whose computed `householdId` matches an existing owner (\u2192 409 via the existing escalation handler), bypassed by `sharesHousehold`; and **wired into `owners.POST.yml`** (a new `household` step between `identity` and `capacity`). Previously it was dead, address-based code.\n- `DetectPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 matches on computed `householdId` and returns early when `sharesHousehold` is set, so a declared member is no longer flagged as a suspected duplicate.\n- `CountNamesakes` \u2014 the \"household-size\" input to the membership level now counts owners sharing the same `householdId` (so a new/sole household still earns the extra tier via the unchanged `MembershipTier` `count==0` rule).\n\n**Kept impact low:** `MembershipTier`, the `Owner.namesakeCount` field, and the `DuplicateHouseholdException` were left untouched (their existing logic still holds under the new meaning), avoiding edits to the wider model/mapper surface. Each changed function is a tiny single-purpose class with minimal surrounding complexity; requests without a postcode short-circuit, so the many no-postcode existing flows are unaffected.",
